  m_text: 'A normal map stores a direction for each pixel. The shader uses it instead of the mesh''s own normals when it computes the light.


    <b>Predict:</b> Move the Point Light around the spheres. Do the bricks react to it? Is the outline of the sphere bumpy?


    <b>Try:</b> Select Point Light - move me and drag it around. Then set the Normal Map strength of the right material to 3, then to 0.


    <size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Textured materials, Walls (Brick)</color></size>'
